  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "haru-e2-and-e6-and-damage-reduction",
      "title": {
        "en": "Haru E2 and E6 and Damage Reduction"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1062_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Haru Anchor Shot, Pointer Move, and Cost Reduction"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Anchor Shot is Haru's Main Damage Source\n2 Cost Scaling Attack at base, but it's best Version is Combo Anchor Shot\nThis Combo is Active as long as you use any Justice/Blue card before using it\nAnchor Pointer has \"Move\"\n\"Move\" transfers the Card directly from zones into Hand\n\"Move\" can transfer from \"Deck\" \"Discard and \"Used\" Pile\n\"Move\" counts as Draw, Only if Moving the card from Deck, not Discard/Used\nAnchor Shot is the reason that Haru uses Justice Memory Set\nBUT If you start to Reduce it's Cost from Divines/Gesture of Freedom\nJustice Set Effect will BREAK since Anchor Shot won't be 2+ Cost\nYou can then use:\nConqueror 1 Cost Anchor Shot\n2/2/2 0 Cost Anchor Shot/Ecstasy Span"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1062_uni3",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1062_uni3",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1062_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Charge Energy and Lift Anchor, Anchor Shot Scaling"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Charge Energy 3 is BROKEN, 70% per Haru card in hand is Insane\n40% The highest Multiplier from Charge Energy is only 144% on Anchor Shot\nThat means Charge 3 only requires 2 Cards 140%, to Break even\nAnything after that is just straight up better\nIt's cap is 630% FOR THE WHOLE TURN, Insane if you can set it up\nYou do need to be able to discard and redraw non Haru cards for this usually\nNia is very good at this, Cassius less so\nLift Anchor is REALLY BAD, It'sDamage, but also ALOT of AP increased\nThe Scaling from Anchor Shot is \"Generic Additive\"\nGeneric Additive is used in the formula after \"Generic Multiplicatives\"\nLike Charge Energy or Lift Anchor"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "E2 Allows Anchor Shot to be played for Left over AP with Damage Reduced\nE2 is 40% FINAL DAMAGE REDUCTION PER MISSING AP\nE6 is 20% FINAL DAMAGE REDUCTION PER MISSING AP\nE2 Examples:\n2 Cost Anchor Shot, Used at 1 AP -40% = 60% Final Damage\n2 Cost Anchor Shot, Used at 0 AP -80% = 20% Final Damage\n3 Cost Anchor Shot, Used at 0 AP -120% = 0% Final Damage\nFunny enough when it comes to Tenacity Dealt, it's based on the Initial Cost\nForbidden Gesture of Freedom/Narja making Anchors 0 cost perma are great\nSince you don't actually lose damage"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-4-patch-notes",
